# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# improvement-loop/ - public by default, small private allowlist
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The default INVERTS here. Everything under improvement-loop/ is tracked unless
# it matches a line below. Do not add reactive exceptions: the allowlist is the
# stated policy (improvement-loop/README.md), not an accretion.
#
# Results: run cells and transcripts. Large, and provider model output.
improvement-loop/verticals/*/results/
improvement-loop/**/transcripts/
# Working artifacts a driver rewrites as it runs: per-repo phase state and the
# model-shared variance scratch. Position is read from the results tree, not these.
improvement-loop/verticals/**/.loop-state.json
improvement-loop/verticals/**/variance/
# The admission-gate cache: machine-written, embeds absolute clone paths, and the
# loop's own instruction is to delete it before trusting a verdict
# (docs/loops/02-repo-admission.md: `rm -rf verticals/<v>/.gate-cells`, then re-run).
improvement-loop/verticals/**/.gate-cells/
# The placement linter carries the private names list it exists to protect, and its
# own header says so: "the names list is itself private, so nothing here is ever
# committed". The .git/hooks shims no-op when it is absent, so a public clone still
# has a working commit path.
improvement-loop/bench/lib/placement-lint.sh
# Journal: candid self-directed reasoning (named losses, cost numbers, self-logged
# bad decisions). A public "how we bench" story is written as a curated doc, never
# by exposing the raw journal.
improvement-loop/verticals/**/LEDGER.md
improvement-loop/docs/**/decision-errors.md

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bench harness (per-run results)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
bench/improvement-loop/results/
bench/analysis/
bench/tools/
bench/CHANGELOG.md
/.council

# Host-built sense indexes staged into the docker build context by
# bench/global/build-prescan.sh. Each one is ~350MB (nextjs.sense) and is
# regenerated on demand from $SENSE_BENCH_ROOT/sense/<repo>/.sense.
bench/global/docker/sense/preindex/

# Local-only bench result snapshots (manual backups before full sweeps).
bench/results.snapshot-*/

# Scenario/rubric backups and invalidated run backups — session-local evidence,
# never published (bench/ scope only).
bench/**/*.bak
bench/**/_invalid*/
bench/results/report-*.md
bench/results/report-for-humans-*.md

# Per-repo variance reports are temporary, model-shared scratch (runs-variance.sh
# overwrites <repo>.md per run); not durable evidence, so kept out of git.
bench/verticals/**/variance/
# Raw codex JSONL is the pre-normalized intermediate (parse-codex-result.py turns
# it into the canonical transcript.json); large, redundant, embeds local paths.
bench/**/codex-raw*.jsonl
bench/drivers/bench-sense-local.sh
/bench/embed-recall

# Per-machine index build-state (built_at timestamps + symbol/edge counts +
# fingerprints), rewritten on every local rescan, so two contributors conflict.
# Untracked: rely on `sense status` for the live fingerprint.
bench/index-state.json

# Local scratch: Python coverage DB and scenario backups taken while
# reworking a seam (e.g. forem.embed.yaml.bak before the reaction rewrite).
bench/lib/.coverage
bench/scenarios/*.bak
.local/
bench/RESCAN-TIMINGS.md
bench/verticals/ruby-rails/results/variance/
/bench/results/loopA-gaps

# vertical-loop.sh per-repo phase state (working artifact)
bench/verticals/**/.loop-state.json
/bench/results/admission-backtest-*
/bench/results/loss-anatomy.md
bench/verticals/go-legacy/
